#. type: Title #
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "UI dimensions (shell / layout / interaction)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:8
msgid ""
"Portal UI is designed along **three orthogonal dimensions**. Visual "
"foundations, components, and interaction patterns all adapt through this "
"lens. Phone size does **not** imply compact layout; Tauri does **not** imply "
"touch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:10
msgid ""
"Agent API tables and hard bans → [`.agent/rules/ui-dimensions.md`]"
"(../../.agent/rules/ui-dimensions.md). Implementation entry points are "
"listed there; this page is the product narrative."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Concept       | What it is                                                                  | Code                                                                       |\n"
"| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Shell**     | Portal runtime host (browser / Tauri; build targets web / desktop / mobile) | `src/portal/app/*`; `portal-sdk` (`getShellKind`, `ShellApi`, buildTarget) |\n"
"| **app frame** | Module rail / bottom tabs, settings chrome                                  | `src/client/app-frame` (`AppFrame`); follows **viewport**, not Shell       |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:19
msgid ""
"Do not call app frame “Shell”. Do not derive rail vs bottom tabs from Shell "
"kind."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "The three dimensions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Dimension       | Controls                                     | Values                          | How decided                                              | Stability                              |\n"
"| --------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Shell**       | Capabilities (native APIs, files, push, IPC) | `web` / `tauri` (+ buildTarget) | Build + runtime (`getShellKind` / `getShellBuildTarget`) | Fixed per install                      |\n"
"| **Layout**      | Presentation (wide/narrow chrome, nav IA)    | `compact` / `expanded`          | CSS `matchMedia` (viewport)                              | Changes with window size               |\n"
"| **Interaction** | Input paradigm                               | `touch` / `pointer`             | `primaryInput` → `(pointer: fine)` + `(hover: hover)`    | Usually stable; can follow peripherals |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:29
msgid ""
"Colloquial “mobile layout / desktop layout” means `compact` / `expanded` — "
"not phone shell / desktop shell."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "Core rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:36
msgid "Dimensions are **orthogonal**: none may imply the other two."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:36
msgid ""
"Forbidden: `isMobile = getShellKind() === \"tauri\"` (or similar mixes)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:36
msgid ""
"Forbidden: one `isMobile` / `isDesktop` flag driving both layout and "
"interaction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:36
msgid ""
"Components pick APIs by responsibility; do not hand-roll `isTauri && "
"matchMedia(...)` to choose menus."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "What each dimension drives"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shell → capabilities (`portal-sdk`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:42
msgid ""
"Use for: file/FS bridges, notifications, Habitat settings visibility, hash "
"navigation quirks, keyboard inset / safe-area host differences."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:44
msgid ""
"Do **not** use Shell kind to lock main nav (rail vs tabs), hover "
"affordances, or Enter-to-send."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:46
msgid "Unsupported capabilities return `null` / `false`; UI degrades."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layout → app frame and page structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:50
msgid ""
"Use for: compact bottom nav + drawer vs expanded rail + multi-column; Dialog "
"vs Sheet **presentation**; list-detail stacking; settings chrome (tabs vs "
"sidebar via `detectSettingsChromePlatform()`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:52
msgid "Common layout patterns:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:57
msgid ""
"**List-Detail** — side-by-side when expanded; stack + route when compact "
"(`ListDetailLayout`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:57
msgid "**Grid-List** — multi-column vs single column"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:57
msgid ""
"**Modal-Sheet** — centered Dialog when expanded; bottom Sheet when compact "
"(presentation = layout; gesture = interaction)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:57
msgid ""
"**Sidebar-Drawer** — fixed sidebar vs hamburger + drawer; compact viewport-"
"fixed layers must clear `--app-bottom-nav-h`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:59
msgid ""
"Settings **section fields** may follow shell "
"(`resolveSettingsContentPlatform()`); settings **chrome** follows layout."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interaction → input paradigm"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:63
msgid ""
"Use for: ContextMenu vs ActionSheet / long-press; hover-revealed actions; "
"Enter send vs newline; minimum hit targets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:65
msgid "Conventions:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:70
msgid ""
"**touch** — hit targets ≥44px; no hover-only affordances; long-press / "
"ActionSheet"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:70
msgid "**pointer** — hover, right-click ContextMenu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:70
msgid ""
"External keyboard on a pad does **not** flip interaction to pointer; "
"strategy stays touch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:70
msgid ""
"Keyboard-open **detection** is interaction; WebView resize differences may "
"use shell helpers (e.g. `useKeyboardInset`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pad example"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:78
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Dimension   | Value                                                    |\n"
"| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Shell       | `web` or `tauri` (how the user opened Portal)            |\n"
"| Layout      | Live viewport (landscape → expanded, portrait → compact) |\n"
"| Interaction | **touch** (`primaryInput: \"touch\"`)                      |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dimension adaptation template"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:82
msgid "When specifying visuals, components, or patterns, document:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:88
msgid "**Dimension-invariant** — shared contract"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:88
msgid "**By layout** — compact vs expanded (or N/A)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:88
msgid "**By interaction** — pointer vs touch (or N/A)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:88
msgid "**By shell** — capability-only differences (or N/A)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: docs/ui/dimensions.md:88
msgid ""
"**Forbidden mixes** — e.g. Shell deciding hover; viewport width deciding "
"ContextMenu vs ActionSheet"
msgstr ""

